# MenuPilot first pilot session + Creations-store discovery - 2026-09-01

Curated from menupilot.log captures (the plugin truncates its log per launch;
launch B overwrote launch A's lines on disk - the batches below were captured
live by audit/menupilot.py before that). Archived batch files sit beside the
log as commands-<n>-*-done.jsonl.

## Launch A (17:28, launch-verify PASS, in-game after autoload)

ping                -> ok runtime=1.7.104.0 ui=1 paused=0 menus_on_stack=2
menu.list           -> 39 registered menus. NO "Creation Club Menu" on this
                       runtime despite clib-ng declaring it; the interesting
                       names: "Mod Manager Menu", "Marketplace Menu".
menu.open Journal Menu  -> MENU_OPEN; query: open=1 has_view=1 swf="Interface/Quest_Journal.swf"
menu.close Journal Menu -> query: open=0 has_view=0            (primitives PROVEN)

menu.open "Marketplace Menu" -> opens... Interface/CreditsMenu.swf. The
  registered "Marketplace Menu" entry is the CREDITS movie: _root.CodeObj
  exposes only closeMenu / getScrollSpeed / requestCredits, Menu_mc holds
  CreditsText_tf. 77 members dumped, nothing store-shaped. Red herring name.

17:29:31 - game crashed ~3s after that dump, while the credits movie was open
  over the in-game state: EXCEPTION_ACCESS_VIOLATION SkyrimSE.exe+059F446
  (ID 442063+0x316) on a background worker thread (null+0x08 read), NOT in
  MenuPilot.dll (crash-2026-09-01-17-29-31.log). Reading: kShow-ing the
  store/credits surface from IN-GAME context runs it without the native
  backing state the engine sets up when IT opens the screen from the main
  menu. Rule adopted: drive store surfaces from the MAIN MENU context, or via
  input-navigation of the engine's own flow, never a cold in-game kShow.

